  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know it's not going to come as a shock to any \nof you watching when I say that the healthcare  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry in America is incredibly broken. \nWe spend almost double most other advanced  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economies and yet we have measurably \nworse outcomes, lower life expectancy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher infant mortality, more easily preventable \ndeaths, far lower early intervention methods,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not to mention the general stress that goes along \nwith the trip to the hospital, which means a lot  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23520,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of people just don't go until it's too late. Now \nagain, I know none of this is shocking to you,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but these frictions, failures, and financial \nincentives have all become so ingrained into a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system that has in turn become so ingrained into \nour country that it raises a rather concerning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39520,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "question. Would it even be possible to unfuck the \nhealth care system without destroying the economy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45760,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the process? The USA is the largest market in \nthe world thanks to the disproportionate share of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our economy dedicated to consumer spending. This \nis a statistic that even I have highlighted here  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before on this channel because it makes us look \nlike we just love buying overpriced trucks and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "useless consumer junk. And while maybe that's \nstill true, if you remove healthcare spending  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from this equation, we are actually right in line \nwith most other pure countries. Put another way,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we actually demolish the health care system and \nbuilt something somewhat efficient in its place,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75440,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we would cut out as much as 10% of our GDP. Now, \n10% of our entire economic output going towards  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spinning the wheels of medical bureaucracy isn't \ngreat. But this broken window still represents  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "millions of jobs, not to mention a lot of our \nfinancial system. They might contribute nothing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of justifying their own existence. But \nnow that they are there, they are extremely hard  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to remove. Now, I know what you might be \nthinking. Just because something is hard  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't mean we shouldn't do it. And even for the \npeople who don't believe in socialized medicine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bureaucratic bloat in healthcare is still a \nproblem. But it's also important to realize that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no policy maker wants to preside over millions of \nlost jobs, even if it would fix one of the biggest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115360,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ongoing burdens on the nation. Oh yeah, and one \nlast thing. Before all of you non-Americans start  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "feeling too smug about the rock and a hard place \nwe have wedged ourselves into, it's probably worth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exploring how we have exported this issue across \nthe world to the point where there is a pretty  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "good chance we are making your health outcomes \nworse as well. I think what's happening today is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually quite important which is is a reflection \nof the uh sprawling bureaucracy that's actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140640,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making America sick. Families have to check their \nbank account before seeing a doctor. The result  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146880,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that manageable conditions go untreated until \nthey become emergencies which is worse of course  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153600,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the patient. Younger Americans die earlier \nthan young people in other developed countries.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That statistics drags down the overall American \nlife expectancy. American men ranked last among  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165840,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 17 countries in that study. Women, by the way, \nwere second to last. Now, before we get into it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think a bit of context is in order. About 5 \nyears ago, I was personally very much a part of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the problem in this industry. I worked as an \ninvestment banker specializing in businesses  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operating specifically in healthcare. The scale of \nthe regulations and business activity that takes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "place in the system between you and your medical \ncareer was big enough that several firms could  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192160,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specialize in just serving these companies. \nThe fact that several investment banks can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be kept afloat just off the fees they charge as a \nmiddleman on transactions between other middlemen  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the medical industry should give you a sense \nof just how much bloat has been piled onto the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "end goal of treating illness. In fact, the broken \nincentives, lobbying, anti-competitive business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "practices, and simple entrenched interest was \npart of the reason why I started this channel  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to begin with. It's easy and honestly a little bit \ncathartic to anthropomorphize the players in this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game and group them into heroes and villains. \nBut to get a good understanding of the problem,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's a lot more productive to follow the simple \nconflicting incentives that have log jammed the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system so badly that it's basically impossible \nto get things done without stepping on someone  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "else's toes. So in the interest of fairness, I \nwant to start with the doctors themselves because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of course typically they get much less blame than \nsomething like an insurance company because well  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know they actually achieve something but they \nstill have incentives of their own and bodies that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lobby aggressively to protect those interests. \nBecoming a doctor and especially a specialist  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "takes a long time and puts most students into a \nmassive amount of debt. According to the AAMC,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the median medical student was graduating \n$25,000 in debt. And that's accounting for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some people who were able to get a scholarship or \nhad parents to fund their education. For students  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going the private college route, that number can \nbe as high as $400,000. To compensate for these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "immense upfront costs and several years \nof loss earnings compared to their peers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's always been the expectation that American \ndoctors are paid extremely well. And on average,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are. Physicians in America are \npaid on average almost double that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of other OECD countries and even extremely \nhigh-income outliers like Switzerland. Oh,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as something of foreshadowing, you might have \nnoticed that Canada is right up there with us. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more on that later. In a lot of other countries, \nbeing a doctor is still a prestigious and highly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "respected job. But it doesn't come with nearly the \nsame expectation of earnings. And in America, this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't by mistake either. The American Medical \nAssociation, which represents physicians, has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lobbyed Congress relentlessly to limit residency \npositions for students graduating from medical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "school. The Medicare graduate medical education \nfunding has remained more or less intact since  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1997. But during that same time, we have added \n70 million people to our population. This has all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limited the supply of doctors to the point where \nthe AAMC estimates that we will have 139,000 fewer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicians than we need by 2033 as our population \ncontinues to age. But on the demand side,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there has been just as much meddling. One of the \nother big pushes by the AMA is to make sure that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are lots of things that can only legally be \ndone by a doctor, even when they could be done by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a nurse practitioner, a physician assistant, or \na non-fysician specialist, like an occupational  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "therapist for a lot of this work. Now, of course, \nsomething like brain surgery should probably  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "require a specialist to be present, but a lot of \nthe tasks that legally only doctors can perform  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really aren't that important or that sensitive. \nOne of the most egregious examples of this scope  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creep is the amount of time that doctors spend \njustifying routine prescriptions and procedures  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to health insurance providers. Now, despite being \nsome more foreshadowing about how bureaucracy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creates bureaucracy, even if this was all totally \nnecessary, most of this work is simple data entry,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which could easily be done by a trained \nreceptionist. But because only doctors are deemed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worthy of these specific tasks, they have to spend \ntheir valuable time filling out online forms,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a cost which is ultimately passed along to their \npatients. America has by far the highest medical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "administration cost per capita anywhere in the \nworld. We spend more than triple the runner up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is Germany and bureaucratic administration \nis basically their cultural identity. Mandated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inefficiency is just one of the causes. A simple \ncombination of bottlenecking the number of doctors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408880,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entering the field and then wasting their time \nonce they are there means that their hours become  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412880,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extremely valuable. Medical schools have realized \nthis which means they can charge more. And even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the doctors themselves who largely do just want \nto help people aren't going to turn down a far  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher than average income because they need it \nto pay off their far higher than average debt.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same goes for things like indemnity insurance, \nlicensing, and training. All of these things can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431680,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be expensive because doctors are paid well. But \ndoctors need to be paid well because everything  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they do to maintain their professional \nstandings is expensive. But all right,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so far all of this is still only counting the \ngroups that do still largely want to help people.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, these little inefficiencies \nhave snowballed into something much larger.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are fewer than a million direct patient \ncare physicians in America, but over 20 million  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people employed by the healthcare industry \nin total, with an alarming share doing very  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little in the way of actually caring for anybody's \nhealth. So, it's time to learn how money works to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find out how it got this bad and why it's become \nalmost impossible to undo. If you've ever looked  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a system like healthcare and wondered why it \nnever seems to change, then this free report from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "HubSpot called Industries Right for Disruption is \nexactly what you should read next. It breaks down  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the industries that are most overdue for major \nchange and explains what's holding them back.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This report covers everything from healthcare and \neducation to real estate and insurance. Basically,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sectors where outdated business models and \nregulation have created massive inefficiencies.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you've ever looked at an industry and thought, \n\"How has nobody fixed this yet?\" This report digs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into exactly that. My favorite section is the \nbreakdown of what makes an industry disruptible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the first place. Things like high customer \nfrustration, fragmented incumbents, and regulatory  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "modes that are starting to crack. It's the kind of \nframework that actually changes how you evaluate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opportunities. Whether you're looking to build \nsomething in one of these spaces, or just want  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to understand where the biggest shifts are coming, \nthis is worth bookmarking. This resource was made  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by HubSpot, who's sponsoring this video. Download \nit for free at the link in my description and see  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what sectors are next. Okay, so another group that \nis often overlooked in this whole equation are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527680,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hospitals themselves. Like a lot of things in \nthe economy, hospitals and practices have become  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another entrenched strain on the system simply \nbecause of how consolidated they have become.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Medical groups have become so dominant in certain \nareas that patients effectively have no other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "options if they want a certain procedure outside \nof traveling several hours. At the same time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546480,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the number of doctors that run their own private \npractice has been consistently shrinking as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the industry pressure has pushed doctors into \nthese collective health systems. Oh, and well,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, I had to bring it up eventually. But the \nGovernment Accountability Office has also pointed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out the role of private equity in strategically \nbuying up regional medical practices to create  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local monopolies on care. Now, anti-competitive \npractices are nothing new in any industry anymore.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The FTC has been infamously flaccid with their \nenforcement for the last 45 years. But the medical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry in particular gets away with a lot more \nthan it should for two specific reasons. The first  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that healthcare is complicated. The average \nregulator hasn't been to medical school to argue  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against industry groups claiming that a merger \nis necessary for patient outcomes. The second  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that the actual costs that come out of these \nmergers are extraordinarily opaque. Of course,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "public enemy number one in this whole game are \nthe private insurance companies. And don't worry,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we will get to them soon enough. But a lot of \nthese combined groups have become so large that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not even insurance providers can push back against \ntheir market power. If a hospital system has a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "monopoly over a critical medical service in an \narea, people will change their insurance if their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "current insurance provider doesn't cover that \nnetwork. Large insurers do have more negotiating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power than individual payers. But if a hospital \nis the only game in town, there really isn't much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can do. This consolidation has also pushed \ninsurers into all or nothing contracts where large  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "health systems will require insurers to include \nall their facilities in their coverage, including  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the expensive ones, or else they won't provide \naccess to any of them. Now, obviously, health  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insurers aren't the victim here. But in certain \nareas, this does prevent them from making a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "narrower network of providers just offering basic \nservices for a potentially more cost-effective  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plan. All or nothing contracts also incentivize \nhospitals to provide services that may not have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been demanded. even by the massively distorted \nmarket since they are being strongarmed into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "covering it anyway. Even for services provided to \npatients on Medicare, there are logical incentives  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that push up prices. One of the key groups that \ndecide how much a medical service should cost  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Medicare is the Specialty Society Relative Value \nScale Update Committee. A bit of a mouthful,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's normally called Ruck. This is a group of \n31 physicians who volunteer to provide guidance on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how to value a physician's work for computing \nhealthcare prices. Now, naturally, a group of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicians would like to say that physicians \nare worth quite a lot. But this group is also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overwhelmingly made up of specialists, creating \na bias that overvalues specialist procedures over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simple primary care. Now, the reason why this \nis important is because the prices this group  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lays out are almost always adopted by Medicare. \nAnd the prices adopted by Medicare act as a price  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "floor template for the rest of the industry as \na whole with various built-in markups. Honestly,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707440,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not too dissimilar to how government \ntreasuries determine the rates that people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711040,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pay on their home loans and credit cards. All \nof these conflicting groups obviously create  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of friction in an already very complex \nindustry, which also allows for other groups  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cash in in ways that are harder to notice with \neverything else going on. Pharmaceutical companies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make roughly 40% of their global revenue here in \nAmerica, even though we have 4% of the world's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730880,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "population. It's no secret that we massively \noverpay for medicine. But within this whole mess,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who's going to notice? The US market has become \nso lucrative that we have effectively subsidized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "R\u0026D for the rest of the world because selling a \nnew drug to Americans is so profitable that every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other country can basically just break even. \nAnd then of course, boxing this whole thing in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are health insurance companies, which may get some \npush back from some of the big health care groups,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but can still ultimately pass everything along \nto regular consumers in costs that are usually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obfiscated by employer healthare plans. These guys \nkeep everything out of sight and out of mind for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most people until they actually need to deal with \nit. And then of course they have an incentive to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "delay, deny, and defend. Even if it did function \nwithout this log jam of conflicting interests,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "healthcare is never going to be a normal market. \nThe information asymmetry is huge. The groups  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paying the bills are rarely the ones receiving \nthe support. Prices are borderline impossible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find. And even if you could get access to \nthis information and actually understand it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789920,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can't shop around while you're dying. Now, \nit certainly doesn't help that the regulators who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should be in there trying to direct this traffic \njam towards something slightly more functional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are being paid off by these various parties to let \nthem get a little bit further ahead in traffic at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the expense of making it impossible to fix the \nsystem as a whole. According to Open Secrets,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the healthc care sector is the number one lobbying \nspender in the country, spending almost 3/4 of a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion dollars in 2024 alone, just at the \nfederal level. But now, the thing is, this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been going on for so long that even if it was \ncompletely fixed and ironed out tomorrow, there is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too much built up in it. Every one of these groups \nemploys tens of thousands of people to negotiate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coordinate, lobby, market to, or just plain old \nsue all of the other groups. Each and every one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of these groups is just trying to serve their \nown self-interest, but none of those interests  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are aligned. And the group that is consistently \nmade to compromise is the patient right in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "middle of everything with the least understanding \nand negotiating power. Another slightly darker  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "visual metaphor is that often rats will get their \ntails caught together. And as they run to try and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free themselves, they only end up pulling the knot \ntighter. Collectively, this administrative bloat  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "built to service the administrative bloat is one \nof the largest employers in the country and at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864480,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "least up until recently has been one of the only \nindustries safe from layoffs. If we could snap our  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869360,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fingers tomorrow and replace our healthcare system \nwith something like what exists in Australia,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873520,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we would lose 7 12% of our economic uh \nproductivity and shed millions of these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jobs. It's also worth noting that Australia's \nsystem is not exactly an unfair comparison.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also have very well-compensated doctors \non average. They have extremely good health  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outcomes and rely on a blended system of private \nhealth insurance and public Medicare. Either way,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this would be a larger hit to both of these \nnumbers than the global financial crisis. However,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900240,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that doesn't mean it's not worth trying because \nover time, this problem is only getting worse. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906080,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "size of the healthcare industry has consistently \nbeen growing faster than the size of the overall  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910400,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economy. By 2033, the Centers for Medicare and \nMedicaid Services predicts that more than 1/5if of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our entire economy will be dedicated to healthcare \nand the apparatus that is built up around it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just like healthcare has slowly grown on the \neconomy, it can also slowly be disassembled over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time as well. Simple things like antitrust \nenforcement, proper lobbying, regulation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more transparency will at the very least deal \nwith the elements that are intentionally trying to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pile more logs into the log jam. We may lose some \njobs like internal auditors for the legal firms,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "servicing the investment banks, managing the deals \nbetween market information providers, giving leads  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945440,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pharmaceutical sales businesses that sell \nthird-party generic substitutes to regional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "healthcare groups. But that's just measuring \nthe uh downsides. One of the biggest hurdles  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to skilled professionals starting businesses of \ntheir own is losing the healthcare security that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes along with being a skilled professional. \nRemoving one of the biggest obstacles to genuine  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business development in the long term would be \nfar healthier for the economy than piling another  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "layer of administration on top of our health \ncare system. Finally, it might also solve what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some consider to be one of the most existential \nproblems in the world. We aren't having enough  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "babies. But when a visit to the hospital can be \nbankrupting, maybe this shouldn't be too shocking,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially to the same group of people who want \nto replace us all with AI anyway. But go and watch  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video next to find out why they still really \nwant you to have a child anyway. because it gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really weird. There was a lot more to talk about \nin this video which I will be writing a newsletter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on in my totally free newsletter compounded daily. \nSo, make sure to sign up for that if you want to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "learn about it more. And don't forget to like and \nsubscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
